From: Rico Lin <rlin@vexxhost.com>
Subject: [PATCH] RBD: Preserve snapshots during volume reimage

Adapt upstream change 995924 to the installed Cinder 28.0.0+a8e.7.10
wheel, preserving its direct-to-RBD creation paths. Reimage downloads
to a temporary file and overwrites the existing RBD image with
qemu-img convert -n -S 0 so its snapshots survive.

Based on the fix by Amit Uniyal <auniyal@redhat.com>.
Upstream-Commit: 3d04f146df28570e58a9a7f405196432a11b2db3
Upstream-Review: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/cinder/+/995924
Closes-Bug: #2160473
Signed-off-by: Rico Lin <rlin@vexxhost.com>
Assisted-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---

diff --git a/cinder/image/image_utils.py b/cinder/image/image_utils.py
